  "_note": "Crop names the question box (विचारा tab) looks for (owner 2026-11-15): the stored questions and answers are for the qa_crops only, so a question that names another crop (and none of the qa_crops) gets a calm 'not in the app yet' line and, when the crop has a guide (crop_guides.json), a button to it, instead of a citrus answer. The names are read from crops.json (labels in mr / hi / en, the en label split at '(' ')' '/', and label_aliases) and crop_guides.json (names), plus the extra names and inflected forms below; other_crops are common crops that are not in crops.json. A word names a crop when it is the name, or the name followed by one of the endings (Devanagari or Latin). skip_slugs are the catch-all entries of crops.json (no crop name). ignore_names are names that also mean something else in a farmer's question and are never read as a crop: केला / केले (Marathi 'did'), आम (Hindi 'common'), बोर (also written for a borewell), gram (the unit), lime (चुना), keli / kela (Marathi 'did'), us (English). Adding a name or a crop needs no code change. not_crop_phrases are phrases in which a crop word names something else (a mulch material, cotton-like wax); their words are never read as a crop. citrus_terms are words of citrus questions that hold another crop's word (lemon butterfly, rough lemon rootstock, the citrus group): they count as santra.",
